comments.message:
Taking this by l-value and then constructing a (malloc'd) temporary into seems odd.

The data flow here is:
1. malloc from a non owning view refManifestDataRaw
2. make two non-owning views of the malloc'd and copy'd data
3. malloc again for each
4. deep copy that malloc'd version into another malloc'd version inside of ReferenceManifestData.

Why not
```
if (reference_manifest.length < 2)
{
    return std::nullopt;
}

std::span<uint8_t> byteView = {reference_manifest_data.ptr, reference_manifest_data.length};
const uint8_t length = byteView[1];
if (length > reference_manifest_data.length) { /* freak out */ }

std::span<uint8_t> vendorID = byteView.subspan(2, length);
std::span<uint8_t> data = byteView.subspan(2 + length, reference_manifest_data.length - 2 - length);

return ReferenceManifestData {byteView[0], vendorID, data};
```

and then change ReferenceManifestData to take random access iterators to uint8_t like data.
